        "description": "Profile round 1 fmod baseline",
        "prompt": "Profile measured round_num=1 of the KernelGen workspace for operator `fmod_tensor_` (in-place torch.fmod_ on Ascend). Use the native kernelgen profile MCP tools (get_profile_context, profile_workloads, record_profile_analysis) against that immutable round snapshot.\n\nContext from the authoritative eval_round result of round 1 (get the exact numbers yourself from the profile context; do not trust my paraphrase):\n- 30/30 correctness PASSED, geo_mean 0.6565, min_speedup 0.508 on fmod_tensor_-timing-3.\n- 9 of the 12 timing workloads measured ~15.9-18.7 us candidate vs ~10.1-11.6 us reference (all small/medium n: 1024 elements up to 1048576 elements).\n- Only 3 workloads are large: timing-3 (0.1627 vs 0.0827 ms), timing-7 (0.1645 vs 0.0847 ms), timing-11 (0.1904 vs 0.1804 ms). Working bytes: fp16/bf16 4096x4096 16.7M elems x2B x(R+W bytes) vs fp32 same count.\n\nThe kernel is a pure elementwise pointwise-kernel: per element it does\n  x = A.to(fp32); y = B.to(fp32); q = x/y; magnitude = floor(abs(q));\n  sign = (bitcast(q,int32) & 0x80000000); sign = where(magnitude==0,0,sign);\n  truncated = bitcast(bitcast(magnitude,int32)|sign, fp32); r = x - truncated*y; A = r\nwith BLOCK=4096 (one program per 4096 elements), fp_fusion disabled, and a cached low-level launcher.\n\nWhat I need from you, with backend-native evidence (OpProf / msprof), and stated separately for a small case (e.g. timing-0/8, 1024 elems) and a large case (timing-3 fp16 and timing-11 fp32):\n1. The measured device kernel duration per workload vs the full-call latency, so I can quantify how much of the small-case ~16 us is host/launch overhead vs device kernel time.\n2. AIV/vector pipe utilization, instruction counts/types if your level allows instruction listing (div vs cvt vs vector-alu), and MTE2/MTE3 activity, to decide whether the large cases are compute-bound (division / fp32-lane throughput) or memory-bound.\n3. Per-program work distribution: how many blocks/programs, whether some cores idle, whether a larger or smaller BLOCK or more programs per core would change occupancy.\n4. Any evidence about whether fp16/bf16 inputs are widened to fp32 in the emitted instructions (this is the main competing hypothesis for the 2x gap on fp16/bf16 large: reference may compute natively in the narrow dtype).\n\nRecord a validated analysis and return exactly one highest-value next experiment for the next round, plus the concrete numbers that justify it. Keep it concise."
      }
